-# Where a record came from: the planting a harvest was picked off, or the one
-# a packet of seed was saved from. One line hanging off the title, so the
-# reader knows what this is part of before scrolling. See DESIGN.md.
-#
-# `verb` is the relationship in the record's own words — "picked from",
-# "saved from".
%p.record-parent.mb-0
  = planting_icon
  = verb
  = link_to planting.display_name, planting
  - if planting.garden.present?
    %span.record-parent-where
      growing in
      = link_to planting.garden.name, planting.garden
